; agg_distinct_1: the aggregate MULTIPLICITY-SEMANTICS witness (owner-directed
; 2026-07-27; docs/Language.md "Aggregation"). Aggregates fold over the
; DISTINCT tuples of the over() projection -- projected COLUMNS, not projected
; rows -- and @invertible vs @recompute is a lowering selector, never a
; semantics change. Pins, via the stdout golden:
;   (1) same-weight collapse: two edges into X carrying the same weight count
;       as ONE under the (X, W) projection (cnt_inv / cnt_rec agree);
;   (2) the count-unique shape: counting ew(_, X2, _) yields the number of
;       UNIQUE X2 values, not the number of rows (cnt_ux);
;   (3) the row-counting recipe: carrying the key column B2 in the over()
;       list counts exact rows (cnt_rows).
; This case DELIBERATELY carries the projected-column lint shape (the _B/_
; wildcards) -- the compiler emits advisory warnings on stderr; the compile
; succeeds and only stdout is golden-compared.
#functor cinv(aggregate i32 Val, summary i32 N) @invertible.
#functor crec(aggregate i32 Val, summary i32 N) @recompute.
#message edge(i32 B, i32 X, i32 W).
#local ew(i32 B, i32 X, i32 W).
#local cnt_inv(i32 X, i32 N).
#local cnt_rec(i32 X, i32 N).
#local cnt_ux(i32 K, i32 N).
#local cnt_rows(i32 X, i32 N).
#query get_inv(free i32 X, free i32 N).
#query get_rec(free i32 X, free i32 N).
#query get_ux(free i32 K, free i32 N).
#query get_rows(free i32 X, free i32 N).

ew(B, X, W) : edge(B, X, W).

; (1) the trap shape: the edge id _B is projected away by the over() list.
cnt_inv(X, N) : cinv(W2, N) over (i32 X, i32 W2) { ew(_B, X, W2) }.
cnt_rec(X, N) : crec(W2, N) over (i32 X, i32 W2) { ew(_B, X, W2) }.

; (2) count-unique: both remaining columns wildcarded; K = 1 pins the group.
cnt_ux(K, N) : cinv(X2, N) over (i32 K, i32 X2) { ew(_, X2, _), K = 1 }.

; (3) the recipe: aggregate over the key column B2; counts exact rows.
cnt_rows(X, N) : cinv(B2, N) over (i32 X, i32 B2) { ew(B2, X, _) }.

get_inv(X, N) : cnt_inv(X, N).
get_rec(X, N) : cnt_rec(X, N).
get_ux(K, N) : cnt_ux(K, N).
get_rows(X, N) : cnt_rows(X, N).
